# Iceland Trip — Dev Rules

## AWS / S3 / CloudFront

- **S3 bucket**: `jerome-dixon.io`
- **CloudFront distribution ID**: `E3MZK5HYTJ14P3`
- **Canonical public URL base**: `https://jerome-dixon.io` (custom domain — use this for ALL photo URLs and asset references)
- **DO NOT** use raw CloudFront domain (`*.cloudfront.net`) — the correct custom domain is `jerome-dixon.io`
- Photo S3 prefix: `iceland_trip/photos/{stop-slug}/`
- App assets prefix: `iceland_trip/`

## Photo URL Construction

Always use this constant in scripts:
```js
const CF = 'https://jerome-dixon.io';
```
Never hardcode a `*.cloudfront.net` domain. If you need to verify the domain, run:
```
aws cloudfront get-distribution --id E3MZK5HYTJ14P3 --query "Distribution.DomainName"
```

## Build & Deploy Sequence

1. `node build-app.js` — injects fresh `route-data.json` into `app.js` (preserves all patches)
2. `aws s3 cp app.js s3://jerome-dixon.io/iceland_trip/app.js`
3. `aws s3 cp route-data.json s3://jerome-dixon.io/iceland_trip/route-data.json`
4. `aws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id E3MZK5HYTJ14P3 --paths "/iceland_trip/*"`

## Photo Matching

- Matching radius: **3 miles** (nearest-stop-wins)
- After adding new stops: run `node rematch-all.js` to redistribute photos
- After rematch: run `node reupload-new-stops.js` to copy photos to canonical S3 paths
- After reupload: run `node cleanup-s3.js --dry-run` then `node cleanup-s3.js` to remove stale files
- Source manifest: `node ... > s3-manifest.txt` keeps S3 index current

## Multi-Project Hosting on jerome-dixon.io

The S3 bucket hosts multiple projects. **Every project prefix needs its own `s3:GetObject` bucket policy statement** — missing it causes silent 403 Forbidden.

Current allowed prefixes:
- `iceland_trip/*`
- `vcu/pgx-risk-calculator/*`

**When adding a new project:**
1. Upload to `s3://jerome-dixon.io/<project-prefix>/`
2. Add statement to bucket policy: `"Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::jerome-dixon.io/<project-prefix>/*"`
3. Verify immediately: `Invoke-WebRequest "https://jerome-dixon.io/<project-prefix>/" -Method Head | Select-Object StatusCode` → must be `200`
4. Invalidate: `aws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id E3MZK5HYTJ14P3 --paths "/<project-prefix>/*"`

## Stop Slug Convention

```js
function slug(name) {
  return name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, '');
}
```
Special Icelandic characters (ð, ó, á, í, ú, þ, æ, ö) are replaced with `-` in slugs and S3 folder names.
